        "merge_commit": "764760381f8e854c6c3c204e417b066af81d229b",
        "note": "限定纳入Harness准入理论：研究自生成prompt、工具和工作流修改怎样在独立审计后持久采纳，并约束参考版本累计退化；并非仅泛泛提到Agent组件。 实证只有合成Monte Carlo统计实验，尚无真实Agent部署评测；保证依赖新鲜独立抽样、参考评估有效性与声明分布，不覆盖任意分布漂移或未测能力。 原文与三轮核验见 docs/internal/reports/maintenance-2026-11-15/。 无HF推荐日，按官方原发表日补刊；first_seen与实际审核日为11/15，不冒充11/15新发表。",
        "owner_login": "adongwanai",
        "promote_to_repo": false,
        "reviewed_at": "2026-11-15T03:29:53.347339+00:00",
        "reviewed_on": "2026-11-15",
        "source_hash": "980bdfa08b52b6e25d4ee07dfd6106297e152ebf21250665a126ea32bf07133e",
        "summary_override": {
          "summary_en": "Develops a theory for persistent adoption of generated prompt, tool and workflow configurations: freeze a candidate, audit it with fresh observations and prespecified metrics, and constrain degradation relative to a reference. Evidence comes from synthetic statistical experiments, not a real-agent study; guarantees depend on sampling, evaluation validity and target-distribution assumptions.",
          "summary_zh": "提出自生成提示、工具和工作流配置的持久准入理论：先冻结候选，再以新鲜审计样本和预定指标决定采纳，并约束相对参考版本的退化。证据来自合成统计实验，尚无真实 Agent 实证；保证受抽样、评估有效性与目标分布假设限制。"
        },
        "week": "2026-W46"
      },
